From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: decode BC through a fragment pass into a compact tiled shadow biblioklept

BC emulation (022) decodes every BC upload with a compute shader into a
LINEAR plane: RGBA8 for BC1/2/3/7, RG16 for BC4/BC5 and RGBA16F for
BC6H. Sampling a LINEAR plane is the main cost when texturing is
bandwidth bound, and the 16-bit planes are 8x the size of the BC data.

On v10+ (CSF), give each 2D BC image an internal colour image
(bc_shadow) bound at the decoded plane's place in the same allocation:
optimal tiling, SAMPLED|COLOR_ATTACHMENT, MUTABLE so the regular
modifier choice applies (AFBC, else U-interleaved). Its format is the
smallest renderable one that holds the decoded data:

  BC4 UNORM/SNORM   -> R8_UNORM/R8_SNORM
  BC5 UNORM/SNORM   -> R8G8_UNORM/R8G8_SNORM
  BC6H UFLOAT       -> B10G11R11_UFLOAT (5/6-bit mantissa, <= 2^-6 rel.)
  BC6H SFLOAT       -> R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT
  BC1/BC2/BC3/BC7   -> R8G8B8A8 (UNORM storage, SRGB view when needed)

The decode is a layered vk_meta rect draw. The existing decoders are
built a second time as fragment shaders (PANVK_BC_FS) and write the
texel to a colour output, so the tile writeback produces the tiled or
AFBC layout and the format packing. vkCmdCopyMemoryToImage (and the
buffer->image copies routed through it) decode straight from the copy
source, so the full barrier between the raw copy and the decode is
gone. Image->image copies and ZERO_INITIALIZED transitions decode from
the raw plane after a narrow barrier.

3D images, v9 and below and PANVK_DEBUG=bc_compute keep the old compute
path. PANVK_DEBUG=bc_wide keeps 16-bit storage for BC4/BC5/BC6H UF.

Mali-G615 MC6, 2048x2048 full chain, ms per 1080p pass, mode E
(3x minified + rotation, one tap, bandwidth bound):

  format    mem MiB      upload ms     E ms
  BC1       24.0 -> 24.8  5.30 -> 3.30  0.544 -> 0.284
  BC3       26.7 -> 27.4  7.04 -> 3.93  0.541 -> 0.289
  BC4       24.0 ->  8.5  4.97 -> 3.43  0.537 -> 0.242
  BC5       26.7 -> 16.6  5.90 -> 5.36  0.540 -> 0.243
  BC6H UF   48.0 -> 27.4 12.90 -> 8.46  1.224 -> 0.321
  BC6H SF   48.0 -> 48.5 14.35 -> 9.32  1.217 -> 0.695
  BC7       26.7 -> 27.4  9.86 -> 5.84  0.598 -> 0.287

Cache-friendly sampling (1:1, 4 taps) stays filter bound at ~0.49 ms.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (0xb8a31030, PAN_ARCH 11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11/022, csf-v11/108
Validation test: tests/dxvk/vulkan/bc/bc_decode.c + bc_verify.py
 (16/16, BC_BC6U_TOL=0.0157; default, bc_compute and bc_wide), device/bc-perf.c
---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/gen_spv.sh b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/gen_spv.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..856eb46c244fdf610ca066a904ddf14f92301df0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/gen_spv.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Regenerate the BC decoder SPIR-V headers (compute + fragment variants).
+set -eu
+cd "$(dirname "$0")"
+for s in s3tc rgtc bc6 bc7; do
+   glslangValidator -V --target-env vulkan1.1 --vn panvk_bc_${s}_spv \
+      -o panvk_bc_${s}_spv.h panvk_bc_${s}.comp
+   glslangValidator -V --target-env vulkan1.1 -S frag -DPANVK_BC_FS \
+      --vn panvk_bc_${s}_fs_spv -o panvk_bc_${s}_fs_spv.h panvk_bc_${s}.comp
+done
+sed -i 's/^const uint32_t/static const uint32_t/' panvk_bc_*_spv.h
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc6.comp b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc6.comp
index 1fb54c066369643783631e94d9535ddba7b1a359..8644ec21c94a39b355ce0a534a2e5aee14ad0f9b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc6.comp
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc6.comp
@@ -2,7 +2,12 @@
 #extension GL_EXT_buffer_reference : require
 #extension GL_EXT_buffer_reference_uvec2 : require
 
+#ifdef PANVK_BC_FS
+/* Fragment variant (-DPANVK_BC_FS -S frag): decode into a colour attachment. */
+layout(location = 0) out vec4 o_color;
+#else
 layout(local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1) in;
+#endif
 
 layout(buffer_reference, std430, buffer_reference_align = 4) readonly buffer InBuf {
     uint data[];
@@ -24,6 +29,8 @@ layout(push_constant) uniform Registers
     int height;
     int depth;
     int format;
+    int x0;
+    int y0;
 } registers;
 
 /* Copyright (c) 2020-2024 Hans-Kristian Arntzen
@@ -791,12 +798,20 @@ DecodedInterpolation decode_bc6_mode30(uvec4 payload, int linear_pixel, int part
 void main()
 {
     int format = registers.format;
+#ifdef PANVK_BC_FS
+    /* One invocation per texel of the render area starting at (x0, y0); the
+     * layer comes from the layered rect draw. */
+    int x = int(gl_FragCoord.x) - registers.x0;
+    int y = int(gl_FragCoord.y) - registers.y0;
+    int z = gl_Layer;
+#else
     int x = int(gl_GlobalInvocationID.x);
     int y = int(gl_GlobalInvocationID.y);
     int z = int(gl_GlobalInvocationID.z);
 
     if (x >= registers.width || y >= registers.height || z >= registers.depth)
         return;
+#endif
 
     ivec2 pixel_coord = ivec2(x, y) % 4;
     int linear_pixel = 4 * pixel_coord.y + pixel_coord.x;
@@ -890,6 +905,10 @@ void main()
             (uint(rgba_result.g) & 0xFFFFu) << 16;
     uint packed_ba = (uint(rgba_result.b) & 0xFFFFu) |
             (0x3C00u << 16);
+#ifdef PANVK_BC_FS
+    o_color = vec4(unpackHalf2x16(packed_rg), unpackHalf2x16(packed_ba));
+#else
     obuf.data[out_word + 2u * uint(x)] = packed_rg;
     obuf.data[out_word + 2u * uint(x) + 1u] = packed_ba;
+#endif
 }
